7wz|a|Having a peculiar, acrid, biting taste, like that of wormwood or an infusion of hops; as, a bitter medicine; bitter as aloes. ; Causing pain or smart; piercing; painful; sharp; severe; as, a bitter cold day. ; Causing, or fitted to cause, pain or distress to the mind; calamitous; poignant. ; Characterized by sharpness, severity, or cruelty; harsh; stern; virulent; as, bitter reproach. ; Mournful; sad; distressing; painful; pitiable. ; To make bitter.	j:1kv,134,3;1iww,101,4;20vx,93,2;o9c,90,3;20vr,88,12;15uf,77,5;243x,69,4;6ul,64,6;s4h,62,2;e89,59,2;1oai,58,2;1eai,53,2;200i,52,1;mas,51,1;qdb,23,3~20vr,88,12;o4i,22,6;6ul,64,6;15uf,77,5;1iww,101,4;243x,69,4;qdb,23,3;o9c,90,3;1ukf,18,3;1kv,134,3;20vx,93,2;1eai,53,2;1oai,58,2;e89,59,2;163a,22,2	e:1vcq,29,3;15u7,21,6;qod,16,1;1xx3,8,6;22p7,7,5~1xx3,8,6;15u7,21,6;22p7,7,5;1vcq,29,3;qod,16,1
