7x7|n|The quality or state of being bitter, sharp, or acrid, in either a literal or figurative sense; implacableness; resentfulness; severity; keenness of reproach or sarcasm; deep distress, grief, or vexation of mind. ; A state of extreme impiety or enmity to God. ; Dangerous error, or schism, tending to draw persons to apostasy.	a:1hig,98,5;yec,96,3;1w1v,5,3~1hig,98,5;yec,96,3;1w1v,5,3	v:1hig,74,1~1hig,74,1	n:200v,132,3;yec,96,3;12l4,53,1~yec,96,3;200v,132,3;12l4,53,1
